<title>SINGAPORE: Asian rice prices - May 2.</title>
<headline>Asian rice prices - May 2.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rice prices quoted on Friday by trading and official sources in the key Asian producing nations of Thailand, Vietnam, Pakistan and India in U.S. dollars/tonne:</p>
<p>								May 2   April 24</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct white B benchmark FOB Bangkok 335-370   330-360</p>
<p>Thailand-100 pct fragrant rice FOB Bangkok     690-700   680-695</p>
<p>India-5.0 pct broken(non-Basmati long grain)FOB 310-315    310</p>
<p>India-10 pct broken FOB (west coast port)	  290	 295</p>
<p>India-15 pct broken FOB (west coast port)	  270	 265</p>
<p>India-25 pct broken FOB (west coast port)	  250	 245</p>
<p>Vietnam-5.0 percent broken FOB Saigon port	 240     225-230</p>
<p>Vietnam-10 percent broken FOB Saigon port	230-235   228-230</p>
<p>Pakistan-Basmati super FOB Pakistan port	 575-590   575-590</p>
<p>Pakistan-IRRI 6 FOB Pakistan port		  225-235   225-235</p>
<p>-- Singapore Newsroom (65-8703305)</p>
